.TH "RAPTOR-EDIT" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-edit \- duplicate elements or copy a block's data
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor edit\fR [\-h] MODEL ACTION ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Structural edits shared with the canvas: duplicate a selection with fresh ids and names, or copy one block's data groups onto others. The model file changes only when the in\-place flag is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBduplicate\fR
copy elements with fresh ids
.TP
\fBpaste\-data\fR
copy block data groups onto blocks
.SH RAPTOR EDIT DUPLICATE
\fBraptor edit duplicate\fR licate [\-h] [\-\-copies N] [\-\-dx T] [\-\-dy T] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}] ELEMENT [ELEMENT ...]
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-copies\fR \fIN\fR
how many copies (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-dx\fR \fIT\fR
each copy's offset to the right, in diagram units (default 40)
.TP
\fB\-\-dy\fR \fIT\fR
each copy's offset downward (default 40)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the result back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR EDIT PASTE\-DATA
\fBraptor edit paste\-data\fR e\-data [\-h] \-\-source BLOCK \-\-targets NAMES [\-\-groups NAMES] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}]
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIBLOCK\fR
the block to copy from
.TP
\fB\-\-targets\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list of blocks
.TP
\fB\-\-groups\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list (default Failure,Repair); see raptor help set\-paths for group names
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the result back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
